# Security

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| Type | Rule |
| Audience | Every specialist that edits product code |
| Adapt | Do not add a product name. Keep these defaults; add project threats in AGENTS.md if needed. |

- Never trust client, worker, or model output. Validate types and paths on
  the server.
- Never hardcode secrets or passwords. Do not commit `.env` or bearer tokens.
- Never log PII, tokens, or full unredacted prompts in new telemetry.
- Parameterized queries only. No shelling out on unvalidated strings.
- Authorization on every mutating or sensitive read. Fail closed (403/deny),
  not empty-success.
- UI: no unsanitized HTML. Framework text nodes only for untrusted data.
- Do not weaken an approval gate or sandbox to “make the agent faster.”
- New dependencies need a one-line HANDOFF note (why existing code cannot do
  it). Prefer zero new deps.
